export anchor ToyBricksStyle:
    number: 104
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Toy bricks
    idea: The dashboard is built from chunky interlocking plastic bricks on a studded baseplate, so every panel, number and progress bar snaps together in primary colours.
    base: light
    palette:
        baseplate: #e9eaec, the page, tiled with #dcdee2 studs every 24px
        brickRed: #c8191f, the current nav brick, the overdue alert and number, Behind chips, white text
        brickBlue: #0b5cad, the top bar, progress studs and this week bars, white text
        brickYellow: #f6c90e, the primary button, the avatar, At risk chips, last week bars and the focus halo, dark text only
        brickGreen: #1e7a3c, the active projects brick and On track chips, white text
        brickWhite: #fbfbf8, panels, nav bricks, the search tile and fields
        ink: #1b1b1b, text and the focus ring
        slate: #4a4d52, meta lines, captions and day letters
    type:
        Two stacks. Display uses Arial Rounded MT Bold, Nunito, Varela
        Round, Trebuchet MS, system-ui in bold. Text uses system-ui, Segoe
        UI, Roboto, Arial. The greeting is 40px at 1.05, summary numbers
        56px, panel titles 24px, project names 19px, body 16px at 1.45,
        meta 14px, chip labels 13px bold.
    layout:
        The page background is a grey baseplate of round studs. The header
        is one long blue brick holding a two brick logo, a smooth white
        search tile, a yellow New project brick, a round white bell stud
        with a red count and a yellow MO stud with the name. Below it the
        nav is a row of small white bricks with their own studs, and the
        current Home brick is red and raised 6px. A wide white plate holds
        the greeting Hi Mara, let's build, the date, and a red brick that
        says 4 tasks are overdue with a cross. The four numbers are bricks
        of lengths 3, 4, 3 and 4 in green, yellow, red and blue. The main
        area has a wide white Projects plate on the left, where each project
        row has a name, a meta line, a status chip brick and a progress
        track filled with blue studs plus the percent. On the right a
        Tasks completed plate shows 14 bars built as stacks of one task
        bricks, yellow for last week and blue for this week, with a small
        stud on top and the value above. An Activity plate lists six items
        with round coloured initial studs. Below 960px the plates stack
        and the numbers go two by two. Below 600px the search drops to its
        own row.
    spacing: A 4px unit on a 24px stud grid. Panels pad 20px, gaps of 12 and 24px.
    density: Medium. Big bricks and clear rows, one project per row.
    corners: 4px on every brick, round studs, round avatar and bell.
    borders: None. Rows divide with a 3px stud grey groove.
    shadows: Each brick has a 6px darker inset lip along its bottom and a hard 3px drop below, with no blur.
    icons:
        Solid filled shapes in currentColor at about 14px. A round stud for
        On track, a triangle for At risk, a square for Behind and a thick
        cross for overdue, always with the word. Studs are a row of round
        bumps along the top edge of each brick in the brick colour.
    focus: A 4px ink outline offset 3px inside a 9px yellow halo, on bricks, fields and rows alike.
    tone: Cheerful build talk, such as Let's build and One brick is one task.
